                "senderName": "NWS Salt Lake City UT",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 16 at 12:01PM MDT until September 16 at 3:00PM MDT by NWS Salt Lake City UT",
                "description": "FFWSLC\n\nThe National Weather Service in Salt Lake City has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSan Juan County in southeastern Utah...\n\n* Until 300 PM MDT.\n\n* At 1201 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 0.25 and 0.75 inches of\nrain have fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 0.5 to 0.75 inches\nin 30 minutes. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of normally dry washes,\nslot canyons, creeks and streams.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of San Juan County including Sei Billikoon, Face\nCanyon Creek, West Canyon Creek, and other drainages and canyons\nbetween the Arizona border and Lake Powell.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "FFWSLC"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WGUS55 KSLC 161801"
                    ],
                    "flashFloodDetection": [
